{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cesfjm9GrAcK7VnvCLnhZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```\n<<PHASE:ANALYSIS>>\n```\n\n**Requirement, restated**\n\nAdd `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` endpoint that sets an order's status to CANCELLED, cancels its CREATED shipments, with idempotent retry semantics, all-or-nothing conflict handling for CONFIRMED shipments, and prevention of shipment creation on cancelled orders.\n\n**Repository findings**\n\n- Order entity (no status): `Order.kt:11-16`\n- OrderController endpoints: `OrderController.kt:15-46`\n- OrderRepository in-memory store: `OrderRepository.kt:10-27`\n- Shipment entity with status enum: `Shipment.kt:9-27` (ShipmentStatus: CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED)\n- ShipmentRepository in-memory store: `ShipmentRepository.kt:10-27`\n- ShipmentController create endpoint: `ShipmentController.kt:26-44`\n- Exception hierarchy: `ApiExceptions.kt:11-30` (ConflictException for 409, ResourceNotFoundException for 404)\n- Error codes: `ApiError.kt:31-37`\n- Global error handling: `GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:13-29`\n- Test patterns: `OrderControllerTest.kt:22-75`, `ShipmentControllerTest.kt:21-84`\n\n**Conventions this repository already has**\n\n- Errors thrown as `ApiException` subclasses (ConflictException, ResourceNotFoundException)\n- Error codes in `ErrorCode` enum (ORDER_NOT_FOUND, ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS, SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS)\n- Controllers return ResponseEntity with status codes (CREATED, OK, conflict/not found via exceptions)\n- Tests use MockMvc with jsonPath assertions checking both status and error envelope shape\n- In-memory repositories use ConcurrentHashMap for thread-safe storage\n- Error responses wrapped in `{ \"error\": { \"code\": \"...\", \"message\": \"...\", \"fields\": [] } }` envelope\n\n**Affected files**\n\n- `Order.kt` — must add `status` field and `OrderStatus` enum (cannot be avoided; order status is core domain state)\n- `OrderController.kt` — must add `cancel()` POST endpoint (cannot be avoided; endpoint is required)\n- `OrderRepository.kt` — must add method to find shipments by orderId (needed to cancel related shipments)\n- `ShipmentRepository.kt` — must add method to find shipments by orderId and optionally filter by status (needed to check for CONFIRMED shipments and cancel CREATED ones)\n- `ShipmentController.kt` — must check if order is CANCELLED before creating shipment (cannot avoid; requirement states shipment creation on cancelled order must return 409)\n- `ApiError.kt` — must add `ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED` error code (needed for 409 when CONFIRMED shipment blocks cancel)\n- `OrderControllerTest.kt` — must add tests for cancel endpoint (required by ticket acceptance criteria)\n\n**Risks**\n\n- **State consistency**: If a cancel operation partially updates shipments before persisting the order status change, the order could end up in an inconsistent state. Must ensure atomic all-or-nothing semantics using a transaction-like pattern (update order status first, then shipments).\n- **Concurrency**: With in-memory ConcurrentHashMap, reading order status and shipment statuses in separate calls could race. Consider reading order once and holding consistent view.\n- **Idempotent retry**: Cancelling a CANCELLED order must succeed without error; implementation must check status before erroring.\n- **ShipmentController dependency**: ShipmentController needs to access OrderRepository to check order status; must inject it.\n\n**Open questions**\n\nNone. Ticket is explicit about all cases: ACTIVE→CANCELLED succeeds with cascade cancellation of CREATED shipments; CANCELLED→CANCELLED succeeds idempotently; ACTIVE with any CONFIRMED shipment→stays ACTIVE and rejects; non-existent order returns 404; shipment creation on CANCELLED order returns 409.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed change, file by file**\n\n1. **Order.kt** — Add `status: OrderStatus` field to `Order` data class. Add `OrderStatus` enum with `ACTIVE` and `CANCELLED` values. Newly created orders default to `ACTIVE`.\n\n2. **OrderController.kt** — Add `cancel()` method annotated with `@PostMapping(\"/{orderId}/cancel\")`. Logic:\n   - Find order by ID, throw `ResourceNotFoundException` if missing\n   - If order status is already `CANCELLED`, return it (idempotent)\n   - Check all shipments for this order; if any is `CONFIRMED`, throw `ConflictException` with `ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED` code and do not persist\n   - If all checks pass, update order to `CANCELLED` status and cancel all `CREATED` shipments\n   - Return the cancelled order\n\n3. **OrderRepository.kt** — No changes needed; the controller can iterate shipments from ShipmentRepository.\n\n4. **ShipmentRepository.kt** — Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` method to return all shipments for an order.\n\n5. **ShipmentController.kt** — Inject `OrderRepository`, modify `create()` to check if the order exists and is not `CANCELLED`; throw `ConflictException` with `ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED` if cancelled. Keep \"order not found\" behavior unchanged (do not throw).\n\n6. **ApiError.kt** — Add `ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED` to `ErrorCode` enum.\n\n7. **OrderControllerTest.kt** — Add tests:\n   - `cancels an ACTIVE order and returns it with CANCELLED status`\n   - `returns 404 when cancelling non-existent order`\n   - `returns 409 when order has CONFIRMED shipment, order stays ACTIVE`\n   - `idempotent: cancelling already CANCELLED order succeeds`\n   - `cancels all CREATED shipments of the order`\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected**\n\n*Alternative: Move order status check into a service layer.* Rejected because the existing codebase has no service layer; all logic is in controllers. Adding a service now would introduce architectural debt inconsistent with the repository. The controller can directly call the repository methods.\n\n*Alternative: Store cancelled shipments separately.* Rejected because `ShipmentStatus.CANCELLED` already exists and can be reused; no need for a separate collection.\n\n**Data and error flow**\n\n1. **Cancel ACTIVE order with no CONFIRMED shipments:**\n   - Request: `POST /orders/O-1/cancel`\n   - Controller reads order, checks not found → return 404\n   - Reads all shipments for order\n   - Checks no shipment is CONFIRMED → pass\n   - Updates order status to CANCELLED in repository\n   - Updates all CREATED shipments to CANCELLED in repository\n   - Response: 200 OK with cancelled order\n\n2. **Cancel order with CONFIRMED shipment:**\n   - Request: `POST /orders/O-1/cancel`\n   - Controller reads order, checks not found → return 404\n   - Reads all shipments for order\n   - Finds CONFIRMED shipment → throw `ConflictException(ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED, message)`\n   - GlobalExceptionHandler catches, returns 409 with error envelope\n   - Response: 409 Conflict with error body, no persistence changes\n\n3. **Cancel already CANCELLED order (idempotent retry):**\n   - Request: `POST /orders/O-1/cancel`\n   - Controller reads order, checks status\n   - Status is CANCELLED → return order as-is without further action\n   - Response: 200 OK with order\n\n4. **Create shipment for CANCELLED order:**\n   - Request: `POST /shipments` with orderId for cancelled order\n   - ShipmentController checks order exists and is not CANCELLED\n   - Order is CANCELLED → throw `ConflictException(ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED, message)`\n   - Response: 409 Conflict with error envelope\n\n**Test strategy**\n\n- **Test 1: Basic cancel of ACTIVE order** — Create order, cancel it, verify response status 200 and order status is CANCELLED\n- **Test 2: Cancel cascades to CREATED shipments** — Create order, create CREATED shipment, cancel order, verify shipment status is CANCELLED\n- **Test 3: Idempotent retry** — Cancel order twice, second call must succeed without error\n- **Test 4: Conflict when CONFIRMED shipment** — Create order, manually insert CONFIRMED shipment (via direct repo call), attempt cancel, verify 409 conflict and no state changes\n- **Test 5: 404 for unknown order** — Cancel non-existent order, verify 404 with error envelope\n- **Test 6: Shipment creation blocked on cancelled order** — Cancel order, attempt to create shipment, verify 409 conflict\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes. Let me start by modifying the Order.kt file to add the status field:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":507,"cache_read_input_tokens":16852,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":507},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c23f6ecc-3b6c-4a17-ba9d-175047de8f62","uuid":"9f6d17f8-2487-4e64-85f6-fc8e8a3b3e01","timestamp":"2026-09-09T09:59:09.875Z","request_id":"req_011CesfjkWpnru6Gx2mhomoe"}
